  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The portfolio contains a facsimile reprint of the edition printed by Fernando Franco de Sarabia in Madrid, Nov. 18, 1954, and a postface written for the reprint edition by Denys Riout.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The preface consists of 3 pages of black, horizontal lines.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Issued in white case (29 cm.) with Yves Klein stamped in gold on front.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Edition limited to 350 copies, not for sale, printed for LVMH (Moët Hennessy-Louis Vuitton) in conjunction with the exhibition "Yves Klein, corps, couleur immatériel" held at the Pompidou Centre in Paris, numbered LVMH 1-LVMH 350. Two hundred copies, numbered 1-200 are reserved for the Archives Yves Klein. Fifty copies, numbered 201-250 are intended for collaborators on the reprint project. There are four hundred copies numbered 251-650.</subfield>
  </datafield>
